 looking at the designs and options for flooring your living spaces, eco-friendly solutions don’t always come to mind. However, there are a variety of such types of floorings depending on your budget.\nThe primary wood used in eco-friendly floors is bamboo. Yet, you can also find those made from recycled materials such as glass, metal, reclaimed wood, ceramic tile, and porcelain.\nIt may even surprise you to learn that there are sustainable carpets on the market too. Some of these use wool, rubber, linoleum, leather, stained concrete, and even cork.\nOverall, linoleum provides some of the most durable sustainable floorings that you can get. Hence, it’s ideal for areas with high foot traffic.\nMost cleaning products contain chemicals meant to kill germs and other disease-causing pathogens in the home. Consequently, they are also comprised of compounds that are known to be hazardous to the environment.\nTheir packaging also turns into plastic waste that’s poorly disposed of by most households.\nIf you’re looking for detergents and cleaning solutions that provide the same hygienic effects but without the possible collateral damage, you can find practical alternatives.\nSuch options are not only effective but even more affordable. Often they come in biodegradable containers that don’t pose the same dangers to the environment even after use.\nFor instance, a startup called Blueland is dedicated to producing dissolvable, reusable cleaning tablets with non-toxic compounds to reduce plastic waste.\nAs more Americans become aware of climate change issues , they are also starting to realize that the heating systems they use in their homes take up a massive amount of energy, most of which is obtained from non-sustainable sources.\nBut what if you can cut down on your household’s energy consumption with an eco-friendly temperature regulating solution?\nThis makes an eco-friendly thermostat a more viable alternative, especially when you consider its unique energy-saving features.\nYou can program these new thermostats to conserve about $150 in energy expenses each year. An excellent example is a thermostat from Nest that supports Amazon’s Alexa voic","tokens":["C","ertain"," products"," that"," we"," use"," in"," our"," everyday"," lives"," can"," exacerb","ate"," climate"," change",","," but"," fortun","ately",","," there"," are"," sustainable"," alternatives","."," Here"," are"," 5"," eco","-","friendly"," products"," that"," you"," can"," use"," instead",".","\n","Research"," shows"," that"," more"," Americans"," are"," now"," aware"," of"," global"," climate"," change"," issues",".","\n","For"," the"," most"," part",","," people"," are"," willing"," to"," make"," some"," changes","."," However",","," not"," many"," are"," ready"," to"," sacrifice"," the"," convenience"," and"," functionality"," that"," technical"," advances"," and"," certain"," products"," provide"," for"," the"," “","greater"," good",".”","\n","Fortunately",","," those"," advances"," didn","’","t"," only"," bring"," problems"," but"," alternative"," solutions"," too","."," Therefore",","," you"," don","’","t"," have"," to"," fore","go"," the"," essential"," benefits"," that"," those"," products"," provide"," since"," you"," can"," now"," get"," sustainable"," alternatives"," for"," most"," of"," them",".","\n","For"," those"," interested"," in"," exploring"," some"," of"," these"," options",","," here"," are"," 5"," eco","-","friendly"," choices"," to"," consider"," today",".","\n","When"," looking"," at"," the"," designs"," and"," options"," for"," floor","ing"," your"," living"," spaces",","," eco","-","friendly"," solutions"," don","’","t"," always"," come"," to"," mind","."," However",","," there"," are"," a"," variety"," of"," such"," types"," of"," floor","ings"," depending"," on"," your"," budget",".","\n","The"," primary"," wood"," used"," in"," eco","-","friendly"," floors"," is"," bamboo","."," Yet",","," you"," can"," also"," find"," those"," made"," from",